From 3bb5c85af01d8dbd9a5f1151a542b8b08705f0db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ttabouch12 <ttabouch12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:14:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 15/21] arm64: dts: exynos7870: Add CPU frequency scaling

Add the CMU_CPUCL0/1 clock controllers, hook the CPU cores up to their
cluster clock and describe one OPP table per cluster, as consumed by
cpufreq-dt. Frequencies and voltages come from the vendor cpufreq DVFS
table (cl0_dvfs_table/cl1_dvfs_table in exynos7870.dtsi of the Samsung
kernel); the highest voltage per frequency is used.

The stock maximum is 1586 MHz. The 1690 and 1794 MHz OPPs that the vendor
kernel can also run are marked turbo-mode, so they are only used once boost
is enabled. The first CPU of each cluster is made a cooling device for
later thermal zone use.

Boards must provide cpu-supply for the CPUs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C7LhHXPfaxZf24zPigwQ9z
